  "relevance_note": "Production-oriented context engineering writeup describing 'context as a compiled view' and handoff translation for multi-agent systems.",
  "reason_included": "Contains concrete context compilation/working-context assembly metaphors (sessions/memory/artifacts -> compiler pipeline -> working context) and handoff translation mechanics.",
  "claim_snippets": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "claim_text": "It proposes treating context as a compiled view: sessions/memory/artifacts are the sources of structured state, flows/processors are the compiler pipeline, and the working context is the compiled view shipped to the LLM for a single invocation.",
      "claim_status": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "claim_text": "The post argues the naive pattern of appending everything into one prompt collapses under cost/latency growth, signal degradation (\"lost in the middle\"), and eventual window overflow.",
      "claim_status": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "claim_text": "For agent handoff, the post describes an active translation: narrative casting of prior assistant messages and explicit attribution/summarisation of tool calls from other agents so the new agent can act on results without misattributing capabilities or history.",
      "claim_status": "asserted"
    }
  ],
